    "text": "Flow control is maintained by following: _ Kevettisemen window size 2. Aersistent Timer > Receiver informs sender about amount of data it can currently buffer using rwnd field in TCP header. a > It helps sender limit its transmission rate, ensuring 1t doesn't exceed the receiver's capacity. TCP uses a sliding window protocol where the sender can transmit multiple segments before receiving an ack. > When receiver acknowledges a segment, it also updates the receive window, reflecting amount of data it can now buffer.",
